-- Q3058: Financial Valuation Methods [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 820-10-35, the WACC used in DCF analysis should reflect the marginal cost of new capital at the target capital structure, not historical or embedded costs. WACC represents the blended return required by all capital providers weighted by their market-value proportions.
Wrong (A): Historical cost of existing capital reflects past financing decisions, not current market conditions relevant to the valuation.
Wrong (B): WACC includes both debt and equity costs; using only equity ignores the tax benefit of debt and overstates the discount rate.
Wrong (D): The prime lending rate is a bank reference rate, not a comprehensive cost of capital reflecting the firm''s specific risk profile.$EXPL$
