  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 820-10-35 and modern portfolio theory, systematic risk (market risk) affects all securities and cannot be eliminated through diversification. It includes macroeconomic factors such as interest rate changes, inflation, and recessions, and is measured by beta in the CAPM.
Wrong (A): Diversification reduces unsystematic (firm-specific) risk, not systematic risk. Even a well-diversified portfolio retains full market exposure.
Wrong (C): Forward contracts hedge specific price or currency exposures but do not eliminate broad market risk affecting all securities.
