  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 815-20-25, Baxter pays fixed 5.5% on the swap and receives SOFR, which offsets the SOFR component of its loan. The net result is a fixed all-in rate of 7.5% (5.5% swap fixed plus 2% spread), making Baxter the fixed-rate payer and floating-rate receiver.
Wrong (B): A floating-rate payer and fixed-rate receiver would be converting fixed-rate debt to variable, which is the opposite of Baxter''s hedging objective.
