  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 815-10-15, a call option on crude oil gives Delta the right but not the obligation to buy at a set strike price. This provides a price ceiling (downside protection) while allowing Delta to benefit from declining prices by letting the option expire. Management pays an upfront premium for this asymmetric payoff.
