  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 815-10-15, an interest rate cap is a series of call options (caplets) on an interest rate index that sets a maximum rate the borrower will pay. If rates exceed the cap, the provider compensates the borrower, while rates below the cap allow the borrower to benefit from lower payments.
Wrong (B): An interest rate floor sets a minimum rate, which benefits the lender by guaranteeing a minimum return, not the borrower seeking rate protection.
